    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0163" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1408: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative of the President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-20T16:00:00-05:00">March 20, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. The following telegram has been received from Bogotá: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Dr. Rodríguez requests you be informed that he shares your view referred
                            to visit of Ocheltree to Tegucigalpa. Braden.”<anchor n="21"
                                xml:id="d213-f1"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>As all three mediators now concur I shall instruct Ocheltree to proceed to
                    Tegucigalpa as authorized in telegraphic instruction number 14, February 17, 8
                    p.m., for purpose suggested in my despatch 683 dated March 16<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d213-f2"/> without the note unless Department instructs
                    otherwise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d213-f1" n="21" xml:id="d213-f1-content">
                <p>Spruille Braden, Ambassador in Colombia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d213-f2" n="22" xml:id="d213-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. It was proposed that Mr. Ocheltree go to Tegucigalpa with technical
                    information to dispel any doubts in the minds of Honduran officials as to the
                    justice of the Mediation Commission’s request.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
